blocks.text:
A newspaper uncovers a government scandal – and is still published the next day. {{1}}
The leadership stays in office for as long as it wants – elections make virtually no difference. {{2}}
A court stops a government plan, and the government complies with the ruling. {{3}}
Critical online posts are deleted, and foreign news sites are blocked. {{4}}
The opposition organises openly and can win the next election. {{5}}
Anyone who publicly criticises the government risks arrest or losing their job. {{6}}
After losing an election, the government hands power over peacefully to the winners. {{7}}
A points system rates people's behaviour – those judged negatively can no longer buy train tickets. {{8}}
